---

<ContentLayout
  title="Ahrefs vs Semrush vs Screaming Frog for Site Audits"
  description="Compare Ahrefs, Semrush and Screaming Frog by deployment, crawl control, evidence, automation, free access and current commercial limits."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  publishDate="2026-03-28"
  updateDate="2026-09-11"
>

<p>Ahrefs and Semrush are cloud audit tools inside broader search platforms. Screaming Frog is a desktop crawler with deeper local configuration and extraction. Choose between them by the audit evidence and operating model you need, then test the same representative URL set in each finalist.</p>

<h2 id="comparison-criteria">Comparison Criteria</h2>

<p>Define required scope, rendering, URL sources, exports, history, scheduling, team access and integrations before comparing plans. Do not compare vendor issue counts or health scores as if they used the same rules.</p>

<h2 id="feature-table">Feature Table</h2>

<div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Ahrefs, Semrush and Screaming Frog audit workflow comparison">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Decision</th><th>Ahrefs Site Audit</th><th>Semrush Site Audit</th><th>Screaming Frog SEO Spider</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Deployment</td><td>Cloud project</td><td>Cloud project</td><td>Windows, macOS or Linux desktop app</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Best-fit workflow</td><td>Stored crawl alongside Ahrefs search data</td><td>Stored crawl inside a Semrush project</td><td>Analyst-led crawl, custom extraction and local exports</td></tr>
      <tr><td>JavaScript</td><td>Documented; configure when needed</td><td>Available under applicable access and settings</td><td>Paid-version feature</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Raw evidence</td><td>Page and Link Explorer plus exports</td><td>Issue and crawled-page reports plus exports</td><td>Detailed tabs and bulk exports</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Repeat runs</td><td>Stored crawl history</td><td>Crawl comparison</td><td>Scheduling and crawl comparison in paid version</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Free access</td><td>Ahrefs Free for verified sites, within allowance</td><td>Limited access; verify current entitlement</td><td>500 URLs per crawl</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Main constraint to test</td><td>Credits, project access and wider subscription fit</td><td>Page, project and rendering allowances</td><td>Machine resources, local operation and licence features</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p><small>Swipe or scroll horizontally to view the full table on smaller screens.</small></p>

<h2 id="pricing-comparison">Pricing Comparison</h2>

<p>Screaming Frog listed a paid licence at £199 per year on 11 September 2026 and a 500-URL free crawl. Ahrefs Free listed 5,000 crawl credits per verified project per month. Semrush described limited Site Audit access and plan-dependent features. These terms can change; compare the <a href="https://ahrefs.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ahrefs</a>, <a href="https://www.semrush.com/pricing/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Semrush</a> and <a href="https://www.screamingfrog.co.uk/seo-spider/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Screaming Frog</a> official pages on the purchase date.</p>

<p>Calculate total cost from pages × crawl frequency, plus projects, users, rendering, API needs and analyst time. Cloud credits and desktop machine capacity are different constraints.</p>

<h2 id="best-for-small-sites">For Small Sites</h2>

<p>Start with Screaming Frog's free crawl when the site stays within 500 URLs and you need a local inventory. Use Ahrefs Free when you can verify ownership and want a recurring cloud crawl. Pair either with <a href="https://search.google.com/search-console/about" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Console</a> for Google's own search and indexing data.</p>

<h2 id="best-for-agencies">For Agencies</h2>

<p>Test client separation, seats, reusable settings, exports, report branding and scheduled delivery. Ahrefs or Semrush may reduce tool switching when the agency already uses that platform. Screaming Frog can provide highly configurable crawl evidence for an independently produced report. See the <a href="/website-audit-tools/agencies/">agency selection workflow</a>.</p>

<h2 id="best-for-enterprise">For Enterprise Sites</h2>

<p>Proof-test segmentation, authentication, rendered pages, crawl safeguards, data retention, APIs and role controls on a representative section. Enterprise requirements may also justify evaluating platforms such as Lumar; vendor category alone does not establish fit.</p>

<h2 id="our-pick">Make the Choice</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Crawl the same controlled URL set with comparable settings.</li>
  <li>Find a known broken link, canonical condition and JavaScript-dependent element.</li>
  <li>Export the affected URLs and hand one finding to an implementer.</li>
  <li>Repeat after a known change and compare how each product shows it.</li>
  <li>Choose the workflow with sufficient evidence and the lowest sustainable total cost.</li>
</ol>

<p>Read the detailed guides for <a href="/website-audit-tools/ahrefs/">Ahrefs</a>, <a href="/website-audit-tools/semrush/">Semrush</a> and <a href="/website-audit-tools/screaming-frog/">Screaming Frog</a>. <small>Product facts checked against official documentation on 11 September 2026.</small></p>

</ContentLayout>
